I am an MPhil Clinical Psychology and RCI-licensed Clinical Psychologist with around 6 years of experience in large-scale mental health programmes, including programme operations, project coordination, implementation, team management, stakeholder management, strategic planning, and collaboration with government and institutional partners.
I am looking for opportunities where I can move into a Project Manager / Programme Manager / Mental Health Programme Lead / Project Coordinator type of role, particularly in the mental health, behavioural health, psychology, employee wellbeing, public health, social impact, CSR, NGO, foundation, healthcare, or government-linked sectors.
Mental health programme/project management
CSR projects focused on mental health, wellbeing, public health or social impact
Programme implementation and operations
Mental health initiatives in NGOs, foundations, hospitals, corporates or social-impact organisations
Government or public-sector mental health programmes
Employee mental health and workplace wellbeing programmes
Large-scale behavioural health or community mental health initiatives
Project planning, monitoring, evaluation and reporting
Team leadership and management of psychologists/mental-health professionals
Stakeholder and partner management
Strategic programme development and execution
Research-to-practice or evidence-based mental health initiatives
I am open to roles where the title is different but the responsibilities substantially involve managing or coordinating mental health programmes, projects, teams, partnerships or large-scale interventions.
My clinical psychology qualification should be considered an important advantage, but I am specifically looking to leverage my clinical background together with my programme-management and leadership experience rather than limiting myself to clinical psychologist roles.
Prioritise opportunities in India, especially Delhi-NCR and major metropolitan cities, while also considering pan-India and hybrid/remote roles where appropriate.
Do not restrict the search only to roles requiring an MBA or traditional project-management background. Consider my clinical psychology training, mental-health sector experience, programme implementation experience, leadership experience and government/institutional stakeholder exposure as relevant transferable experience.
My preferred compensation is approximately ₹20 lakh per annum (₹20 LPA) or above. However, I am flexible on compensation for a particularly strong role, especially where the position offers significant project/programme ownership, leadership responsibility, career growth, strong organisational exposure, or opportunities to work on large-scale mental health or social-impact initiatives.
Do not automatically exclude roles below ₹20 LPA if they are a strong match for my experience and career direction. Prioritise roles that are reasonably aligned with my compensation expectations.
